Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sqlite-worker): retire a failed actor before
 reopening (temporary, completes backport of #170138)

c0ba37ed20 ported only the sqlite-store.ts half of #170138, so a Workboard
facade reopened onto the same actor whenever another client still retained it.
That actor stays in the broker map and rethrows its slot failure, so board
writes kept failing with "database is locked" until a gateway restart
(1.11.2026 and 7.11.2026). Silent sibling facades hold exactly that reference.

Retire the failed actor before reopening, as upstream 069d40e40c does. Adds a
recovery test with a silent sibling, and a guard that one real SQLite lock does
not reopen the store.

TEMPORARY: remove once we run a release containing openclaw/openclaw#170138
(first in v2026.10.10-beta.1), together with c0ba37ed20.
